# Direct input to the WINDOWS + CUDA lock. Regenerate it with:
#   uv pip compile env/requirements-win-cuda.in --generate-hashes \
#       --python-version 3.13 --python-platform x86_64-pc-windows-msvc \
#       --extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu130 \
#       --index-strategy unsafe-best-match --emit-index-url \
#       -o env/requirements-win-cuda.lock.txt
#
# Two things differ from env/requirements.in, and only two:
#
#   torch is +cu130, from download.pytorch.org. The torch on PyPI is CPU-only on
#   Windows, so installing the plain lock there gives a working import and no GPU.
#
#   mtlflashattn is absent. It is the Metal attention kernel; it has no meaning
#   off Apple Silicon, and the profile that requires it (comfyui-yue2-mps-v1)
#   refuses to load on Windows anyway. Windows runs the 'official' profile, which
#   means no continuation and no chunking - see README.
#
# Everything else is the same pin. Keep the two files in step by hand: a version
# that moves in one and not the other is two different programs.
#
# yue2-infer is NOT here: it installs from the commit pinned in pins.env.
